delegate. Either way, awaiting inside asyncio.run works.\n\nFinal check on assertion in test 2: `str(q)` after two put_nowait and two task_done \u2192 `\"<Queue maxsize=0 queue=deque(['a', 'b'])>\"`. \u2713.\n\nAlso, in test 2, maxsize=0 means unbounded \u2014 `full()` returns False always. put_nowait works. \u2713.\n\nWrite it out:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Coverage tests for tornado.queues.Queue._format (lines 337-346).\n\nEach test drives ``Queue.__str__``/``Queue.__repr__`` (which call\n``_format``) through a different internal state so that every line and\nbranch of ``_format`` is executed:\n\n* line 337: always executed on any ``str(q)``/``repr(q)``;\n* lines 338-339: both an empty and a non-empty internal ``_queue``;\n* lines 340-341: a getter parked on an empty queue;\n* lines 342-343: a putter parked on a full queue;\n* lines 344-345: both zero and non-zero ``_unfinished_tasks``.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\n\nfrom tornado.queues import Queue\n\n\ndef test_str_empty_queue_only_shows_maxsize():\n    # Empty queue: only the \"maxsize=\" part is produced (false branches\n    # of the ifs on lines 338, 340, 342 and 344).\n    q = Queue(maxsize=3)\n    assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=3>\"\n    s = str(q)\n    assert \"queue=\" not in s\n    assert \"getters[\" not in s\n    assert \"putters[\" not in s\n    assert \"tasks=\" not in s\n    # __repr__ goes through _format as well.\n    assert repr(q) == \"<Queue at %s maxsize=3>\" % hex(id(q))\n\n\ndef test_str_with_items_and_unfinished_tasks():\n    # Non-empty _queue (lines 338-339) and unfinished tasks (344-345).\n    q = Queue(maxsize=0)\n    q.put_nowait(\"a\")\n    q.put_nowait(\"b\")\n    assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=0 queue=deque(['a', 'b']) tasks=2>\"\n    # task_done() decrements _unfinished_tasks, shrinking the output.\n    q.task_done()\n    assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=0 queue=deque(['a', 'b']) tasks=1>\"\n    # Once all tasks are done the \"tasks=\" part disappears again.\n    q.task_done()\n    assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=0 queue=deque(['a', 'b'])>\"\n    assert \"tasks=\" not in str(q)\n\n\ndef test_str_with_waiting_getter():\n    async def main():\n        q = Queue(maxsize=1)\n        # An empty queue makes get() park a future in _getters (340-341).\n        getter = q.get()\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1 getters[1]>\"\n        assert \"putters[\" not in str(q)\n        # Putting an item hands it straight to the parked getter.\n        q.put_nowait(\"x\")\n        assert await getter == \"x\"\n        # The getter is gone; the handed-over item left an unfinished task.\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1 tasks=1>\"\n        q.task_done()  # clean up the queue state\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1>\"\n\n    asyncio.run(main())\n\n\ndef test_str_with_waiting_putter():\n    async def main():\n        q = Queue(maxsize=1)\n        q.put_nowait(\"a\")  # fills the queue and registers an unfinished task\n        # A full queue makes put() park (item, future) in _putters (342-343).\n        putter = q.put(\"b\")\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1 queue=deque(['a']) putters[1] tasks=1>\"\n        assert \"getters[\" not in str(q)\n        # Taking an item resolves the parked putter.\n        assert await q.get() == \"a\"\n        assert await putter is None\n        # The parked item \"b\" was never enqueued, so the queue is now empty\n        # and only the unfinished task from \"a\" remains.\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1 tasks=1>\"\n        q.task_done()  # clean up the queue state\n        assert str(q) == \"<Queue maxsize=1>\"\n\n    asyncio.run(main())\n```\n\nWait \u2014 in test 4, after `await q.get()`, is `_unfinished_tasks` 1? `put_nowait(\"a\")` \u2192 `__put_internal` \u2192 `_unfinished_tasks += 1` \u2192 1. The parked putter's \"b\" never went through `__put_internal`. `get_nowait` popping the putter doesn't change `_unfinished_tasks`. So yes, 1. \u2713.\n\nHmm, but wait: does `get_n